Every Azure solution requires architectural decisions that balance performance, security, availability, scalability, and cost. A structured decision framework helps architects evaluate available options objectively.

Important decision criteria include:

* Business requirements
* Security needs
* Compliance obligations
* Expected workload
* Performance targets
* Budget limitations
* Future growth

For example, an organisation designing a customer portal may choose managed services over virtual machines to reduce operational complexity.

A real-life use case is architecture review boards evaluating proposed Azure solutions before production implementation.

Structured decision-making improves solution quality and long-term maintainability.
